>
  <KeyTakeaways
    items={[
      'Atumelnant (CRN04894) is a once-daily oral small molecule that blocks MC2R, the receptor through which ACTH drives the adrenal cortex. It is the first clinical drug built to do that.',
      'Its lead indication is classic congenital adrenal hyperplasia, where excess ACTH pushes the gland to overproduce androgens. ACTH-dependent Cushing’s is the second programme.',
